   930 				; Menu_Ramp_Set - Reg1 = menu palette set 1-3.  Sets 1-3 are pure single-
   931 				; component ramps - set 1 colour i = (i,0,0), set 2 = (0,i,0), set 3 = (0,0,i)
   932 				; - so they are generated straight into the registers rather than stored.
   933 				; Y walks CR/CG/CB (consecutive registers) for each colour; the component
   934 				; whose register matches the set gets i, the other two get 0.  Plain
   935 				; sta (VBXEBase),y (what vbsta expands to) so Y can be the register index.
   936 				; Also used by Load_Pal (palette keys on the menu's P screen).
   937 3673			Menu_Ramp_Set
   938 3673 A5 80			lda Reg1
   939 3675				vbsta VBXE_PSEL
