  1159 				;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
  1160 				; Pal_Preview_Init - boot-time build of the P key's palette screen in its own
  1161 				; VRAM (PAL_PREVIEW_VRAM / PAL_PREVIEW_CRAM, zeroed by clear_vbxe).  The
  1162 				; squares and cells are the same for every image - only the palette registers
  1163 				; differ - so P and ESC just re-point XDL_Image_Attribute (Set_Attr_Source_*)
  1164 				; and the image underneath is never touched.  Runs after Build_Menu_Ramp_Table.
  1165 				; BLT_SETUP_CMAP_1's destination is patched to PAL_PREVIEW_CRAM for the one
  1166 				; expand, then put back to $017003 for Load_Image.  $14000 is left dirty -
  1167 				; harmless, Load_Image rewrites all of it and Clear_Screen zeroes it.
  1168 				;-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
